{ isc_vars - the ISC's read-only tables (a DSEE derived object of the
  iscg_input description; cc.a88k only): no code and no module data;
  the unit defines the sections isc_tool_generated_readonly_tables
  (0x2BC13C, 3264 bytes: each rule's result kind, by rule 1..563, then
  the six opcode maps by il$t: hard_work and the pass-1 actions read
  them) and isc_readonly_tables (0x2BCDFC, 3120 bytes: the ISC's own
  tables, isc_user_routines' views in isc_types.ins.pas), the variables
  isc.pvt.pas and isc_types.ins.pas declare in them, with `define'
  statements (the language reference's section 7.2.2, method 2; the
  scheme of docs/questions.md 161).  It opens isc_var_defines.ins.pas
  first (its .blocks list).

  Generated by tools/iscg_gen.py from the rule file
  (moon_unit/isc_prism_dervobjs/dseeaggs/iscg_input/rules/*.isc): do not
  edit; change the rule file or the generator's fixed text
  (tools/iscg_text.py) and regenerate.  tools/iscg_gen.py --check (in
  the gate) fails when this file and the rule file disagree.

  The image's record lists the back end's other named sections too
  (amse_premod_immed_low .. instruction_assembly: backend.ins.pas
  declares them, asm, lst and tm_utils define them).  The two sections'
  variables are named as the sections: dpc gap 32 (docs/dpc-gaps.md
  32; the gate renames them).

  Not known from the original: the tables' structure inside
  isc_readonly_tables (written as words), the opcode maps' names. }
